      "theory_name": "Irrelevant Sound Effect (ISE) / Changing-State Hypothesis",
      "commitment_type": "tests",
      "specific_claim": "Changing-state auditory stimuli disrupt memory performance more than steady-state stimuli or silence, due to interference with attentional or working memory processes. This paper investigates its impact on visual memory retrieval."
    }
